# Agent Instructions

## Project Shape

- Package lives under `src/__SPECX_PACKAGE_NAME__`.
- The starter core behavior lives under `src/__SPECX_PACKAGE_NAME__/core/health/`.
- Add further application behavior under `src/__SPECX_PACKAGE_NAME__/core/<scope>/`.
- Delivery belongs under `src/__SPECX_PACKAGE_NAME__/delivery/<framework>/` and remains
  separate from core behavior when a delivery technology is added.
- Scope-owned technical adapters belong under
  `src/__SPECX_PACKAGE_NAME__/core/<scope>/infrastructure/<technology>/`.
- Shared technical resources belong under `src/__SPECX_PACKAGE_NAME__/infrastructure/`.
- DI composition lives in `src/__SPECX_PACKAGE_NAME__/ioc/container.py`.

## Entrypoints

- DI composition: `src/__SPECX_PACKAGE_NAME__/ioc/container.py`
- Starter use case: `health/check-health`
- Add framework-specific runtime entrypoints here when they exist.

## Commands

- Install: `uv sync --locked --all-groups`
- Full check: `make check`
- Lint/type/format/architecture check: `make lint`
- Format/fix: `make format`
- Tests: `make test`
- Architecture diagnostics: `uv run --locked specx check --output-format json`
- List core components: `uv run --locked specx project component list --output-format json`
- List use cases: `uv run --locked specx project use-case list --output-format json`
- Show one use case: `uv run --locked specx project use-case show health/check-health --output-format json`
- Run a query use case: `uv run --locked specx project use-case run health/check-health`
- Preview a scaffold: `uv run --locked specx project use-case create <component>/<name> --kind query --dry-run --output-format json`
- Use `uv run --locked specx project --error-format json ...` when an agent must parse failures.

## Working Agreement

- Inspect the existing project shape and commands before changing code.
- Use the project CLI for component and use-case discovery or scaffolding.
- Run `uv run --locked specx check --output-format json`, follow each diagnostic's `hint`
  and `documentation_url`, then finish with `make check`.
- Architecture policy lives in executable specx, Ruff, type, and test checks. Do not copy
  generic policy into this file.
